      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4489713140": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-11-19T02:39:04.560446+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "This is a Fully Remote Job\nAbout Our Client:\nThe organization operates in the technology sector, focusing on developing software solutions that meet project requirements and improve existing systems. It addresses the challenge of building reliable, scalable, and efficient technology by applying strong software development principles and collaborative engineering practices. The organization emphasizes practical software development and continuous learning within a team environment.\nAbout the Opportunity:\nThe SOFTWARE DEVELOPER is responsible for contributing to the development, testing, and maintenance of software applications. This role supports the organization by applying programming knowledge and problem-solving skills to build and enhance software solutions that meet business objectives. It offers an opportunity to work on real-world technical challenges and develop practical software products while growing technical expertise.\nResponsibilities:\nDevelop, test, debug, and maintain software applications based on project requirements.\nWrite clean, efficient, reusable, and maintainable code following best practices.\nCollaborate with developers and cross-functional team members to design and implement features.\nUse programming languages such as Python, Java, JavaScript, or TypeScript.\nAssist in developing and integrating REST APIs and web application components.\nWork with databases and SQL to manage application data.\nIdentify and troubleshoot software defects and performance issues.\nParticipate in code reviews and incorporate feedback.\nUse Git and GitHub for version control.\nWrite and execute unit tests to ensure software reliability.\nDocument technical processes, features, and workflows.\nLearn and apply new tools, frameworks, and technologies.\nRequirements:\nMaster's degree in Computer Science, Software Engineering, Information Technology, Computer Engineering, or related field.\n0–1 year of experience in Software Engineering, Software Development, or related role.\nStrong understanding of programming fundamentals and object-oriented programming.\nProficiency in at least one programming language such as Python, Java, JavaScript, or TypeScript.\nFamiliarity with data structures and algorithms.\nUnderstanding of REST APIs and web application fundamentals.\nFamiliarity with SQL, relational databases, and basic database concepts.\nExperience using Git and GitHub for version control.\nUnderstanding of software development life cycle principles.\nFamiliarity with debugging, testing, and writing maintainable code.\nStrong analytical thinking and problem-solving abilities.\nAbility to learn new technologies and adapt to project requirements.\nStrong communication, teamwork, and collaboration skills.\nMotivation to build reliable software and continuously improve technical skills.\nPay Range and Compensation Package:\nThe pay range and compensation package for this role will be determined based on the candidate's experience, skills, and other relevant factors.\nAbout the Opportunity (Preferred Qualifications):\nExperience with academic, internship, or personal software development projects.\nFamiliarity with frontend frameworks like React or backend frameworks like Node.js, Django, or Spring Boot.\nBasic knowledge of cloud platforms, software deployment, or CI/CD.\nFamiliarity with Agile development and collaborative workflows.\nOpportunity to work with modern development tools and engineering practices.\nCollaborative environment promoting knowledge sharing and continuous learning.\nOpportunities for professional development and career growth.\nEqual Opportunity Statement: Our client is an equal opportunity employer. They celebrate diversity and are committed to creating an inclusive environment for all employees. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, gender, gender identity or expression, sexual orientation, or national origin.\nNote:\nTalentHop is a recruitment partner of this role. Please note that all employment decisions, including candidate assessment, interviews, hiring, compensation, and employment terms, are made exclusively by the hiring employer.",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4489793450": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-11-19T02:39:04.560446+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "Job Overview:\nWe are looking for a Healthcare Integration Engineer to streamline client communication and support the delivery of HL7 and FHIR integration projects. Bridging the gap between clients and engineering teams, translate healthcare workflows into technical requirements, and troubleshoot complex integration issues.\nThe ideal candidate combines strong healthcare domain knowledge with analytical, debugging, and communication skills, alongside hands-on experience with .NET, C#, OAuth, and T-SQL.\nJob Responsibilities:\nServe as a technical point of contact for clients on HL7 and FHIR projects, communicating requirements, progress, issues, and resolutions clearly.\nCollaborate with clients to understand clinical workflows, integration requirements, and data exchange needs.\nDocument business requirements, technical specifications, interface configurations, data mappings, and acceptance criteria.\nDevelop, maintain, and troubleshoot healthcare interfaces and APIs using C# and ASP.NET Core.\nAnalyze integration data, application logs, and database records to identify discrepancies, troubleshoot issues, and determine root causes.\nInvestigate issues involving message processing, data validation, connectivity, authentication, and authorization.\nValidate integrations, coordinate testing activities, and resolve client-reported technical issues.\nWrite and optimize T-SQL queries and stored procedures to support data analysis and troubleshooting.\nSupport integration testing, client acceptance testing, go-live activities, and post-launch issue resolution.\nMaintain clear documentation of interface configurations, technical decisions, and troubleshooting procedures.\nQualifications:\nBachelor’s degree in Computer Science, Software Engineering, or a related field.\n02 - 03 years of experience in software development in Microsoft based, one or more general-purpose programming languages.\nKnowledge of healthcare interoperability standards, particularly HL7 v2 and FHIR.\nUnderstanding of healthcare workflows and electronic health record systems.\nHands-on experience with C#, .NET, ASP.NET Core, and RESTful APIs.\nWorking knowledge of OAuth and secure API authentication and authorization.\nProficiency with Microsoft SQL Server and T-SQL.\nAnalytical and debugging skills, including the ability to trace issues across applications, interfaces, and databases.\nAbility to communicate technical concepts clearly to technical and nontechnical stakeholders.\nAbility to gather requirements, lead technical discussions, and coordinate issue resolution with clients.\nExperience with healthcare interface engines is preferred.\nFamiliarity with Git and collaborative software development practices.\nFamiliarity with SMART on FHIR, terminology standards, and healthcare data mapping.\nFamiliarity with CI/CD tools and practices.\nCompensation & Benefits:\n💰 Financial:\nCompetitive salary and bi-annual bonus.\nFast track and uncapped career growth for high performers.\nCompany-sponsored vehicle financing (car and bike).\nInterest-free loans.\nProvident Fund: CureMD matches up to 8% of your base salary.\n🏥 Health and Wellness:\nIn-house clinic with a team of certified male and female doctors with 24/7 telemedicine service.\nHospital treatment monitoring by company doctors.\nComprehensive health coverage for your immediate family (outpatient, inpatient, maternity and parents' inpatient).\nExclusive health benefits and discounts at top class clinics and labs.\n🤝🏻 Supportive Workplace:\nPick-up and drop-off services for female employees.\nIn-house daycare facility.\nIn-house gym and recreational area to unwind.\n📚 Continued Learning:\nCompany-sponsored trainings, workshops, development programs and retreats.\nPaid specialized trainings/certifications.\nThe Difference You’ll Make:\nAt CureMD, every role, whether senior or junior, plays a pivotal part in transforming healthcare. By joining our innovative team, you’ll contribute to groundbreaking technology that directly impacts patient care, enhances healthcare efficiency, and saves lives globally. Your skills and passion will drive meaningful change, helping us deliver solutions that support healthcare professionals in critical, real-time settings. Together, we’re not just advancing technology — we’re making a tangible difference in people’s lives. Together, let’s save lives.",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      }
    },
    "updated_at": "2026-11-19T02:39:04.560446+00:00"
  },
