      "https://www.linkedin.com/posts/josephcass_breaking-brookfield-announces-huge-27-billion-share-7523323322541969408-zmpB": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-11-19T02:39:50.750502+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "status": "active",
          "text": "BREAKING: Brookfield announces HUGE $27 BILLION AI data centre project in the UK! \n\nBrookfield has partnered with British energy company Drax Group and AI business Radiant to develop one of the UK’s largest AI data centres at Drax Power Station in the north of England. \n\nBloomberg reports that the project could attract more than $27 Billion billion in investment, with an initial $3.3 Billion planned for the first phase, backed by Brookfield’s partnership with the Qatar Investment Authority.\n\nThe idea is to build the data centre alongside an existing power station, giving it access to the enormous amounts of electricity needed to run AI technology. Drax CEO Will Gardiner said: “If constructed in full, this project could become one of the largest data centres in the UK.” Brookfield's Connor Teskey recently said of AI infrastructure: \"there is no shortage of capital - and there is no shortage of demand.\"\n\nBig news for European AI infrastructure!\n\nFollow Joseph Cass for finance news and insights.",
          "posted_at": "2026-11-03T10:00:57.048Z"
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/posts/trmlabs_at-2005-utc-on-october-29-approximately-activity-7521757016516628480-UBCU": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-11-19T02:39:50.750502+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "status": "active",
          "text": "At 20:05 UTC on October 29, approximately USD 6.36 billion began moving out of Binance wallets across ten blockchains, most of it in about 20 minutes. It is the largest crypto theft on record, roughly four times the Bybit hack of February 2025.\n\nTRM Labs attributes the attack to TraderTraitor, North Korea’s elite state-sponsored hacking unit, based on robust on-chain and off-chain intelligence. The same group was named by the FBI in the Bybit hack, and the staging, the Tornado Cash funding and the pre-signed transactions all match earlier North Korea-linked heists.\n\nThe response has been fast. Tether, Circle, Ripple, World Liberty Financial and Arbitrum’s Security Council have frozen roughly USD 2.7 billion. But the attacker still controls about USD 2.4 billion in assets beyond any issuer’s reach, and is racing to convert and move them.\n\nTRM continues to work with Binance and the Beacon Network to track the funds and alert partners in real time. The story is still developing, and we will share more as the investigation unfolds.\n\nRead our full analysis: https://lnkd.in/e-9KjvPB",
          "posted_at": "2026-10-30T02:17:00.224Z"
        }
      },
      "https://pe.linkedin.com/posts/js-investments-limited_position-senior-dot-net-developer-location-activity-7212353489551712261-Igb4": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-11-18T20:40:09.105527+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "status": "active",
          "text": "Position: Senior Dot Net Developer\n\nLocation: Karachi\n\nJob Role Summary:\nAs a Senior Dot NET Developer, you will be supporting the development and maintenance of software solutions tailored to the specific needs of asset management operations. You will work closely with teams to understand business requirements and translate them into functional software components.\n \nKey Responsibilities:\n- Design, code, test and manage various applications.\n\n- Follow outlined standards of quality related to code and systems.\n\n- Develop automated tests and conduct performance-tuning.\n\n- Developing web-based applications in .NET, Angular, C#, HTML, JavaScript, ASP.\n\n- Working with MS SQL Server and MySQL. \n\nEducation:\nBachelor's degree in Computer Science or relevant field.\n\nExperience:\n4 to 5 years of experience utilizing the .NET software framework.\nInterested candidates can apply at careers@jsil.com mentioning “Senior Dot Net Developer” in the email subject line.",
          "posted_at": "2024-06-28T07:17:50.918Z"
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/posts/aimnode-technologies_job-title-nodejs-developer-location-karachi-activity-7176828931122053120-mDsE": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-11-18T20:40:09.105527+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "status": "active",
          "text": "Job Title: Node.js Developer\nLocation: Karachi\nCompany: AimNode Technologies\nJob Type: Full-time\n\nJob Description:\nWe are seeking a talented Node.js Developer to join our team. As a Node.js Developer, you will be responsible for designing and implementing server-side web application logic, as well as integrating user-facing elements developed by front-end developers. You should have a strong understanding of JavaScript and asynchronous programming. The ideal candidate is passionate about building scalable, high-performance web applications using Node.js and related technologies.\n\nResponsibilities:\n- Develop and maintain server-side logic using Node.js\n- Design and implement RESTful APIs for web services\n- Collaborate with front-end developers to integrate user-facing elements with server-side logic\n- Optimize application performance for maximum speed and scalability\n- Implement security and data protection measures\n- Write clean, maintainable, and testable code\n- Stay up-to-date with emerging technologies and best practices\n\nRequirements:\n- Proven experience as a Node.js Developer or similar role\n- Strong proficiency in JavaScript and asynchronous programming\n- Experience with Node.js frameworks such as Express.js or Koa.js\n- Knowledge of database technologies such as MongoDB, MySQL, or PostgreSQL\n- Familiarity with front-end technologies such as HTML, CSS, and JavaScript\n- Experience with version control systems (e.g., Git)\n- Excellent problem-solving and communication skills\n- Bachelor's degree in Computer Science, Engineering, or a related field (preferred)\n\nHow to Apply:\nInterested candidates should submit their resume, along with a cover letter detailing their relevant experience and why they are a good fit for the position. Please also include links to any relevant portfolios or projects. Applications can be sent to devawaisdeveloper@gmail.com with the subject line \"Node.js Developer.\"",
          "posted_at": "2024-03-22T06:35:56.173Z"
        }
      },
